    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is centered on **Corbin Carroll** (75.70) and **Seiya Suzuki** (71.14), who represent our clearest paths to production. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive situational bump due to Kevin Gausman\u2019s slow delivery, which creates an ideal environment for him to exploit the stolen base category\u2014our highest priority. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** earns a top-tier grade by drawing a favorable matchup against the hittable Merrill Kelly; with an SP_xERA of 5.27, Kelly provides the soft landing **Seiya Suzuki** needs to drive both average and counting stats. **Henry Bolte** (61.01) also earns a start as our leadoff hitter, buoyed by a +10% order bonus and a park factor that favors his profile against the middling Zebby Matthews.\n\nManaging our depth remains a tightrope walk given the game cap constraints. The most difficult omission today is **Griffin Conine** (35.44), who fell short of the start threshold due to a difficult matchup against Ranger Suarez and a detrimental platoon disadvantage (L/L). While **Griffin Conine** flashed potential with an excellent xwOBA, the optimizer prioritized the higher floor offered by **Mickey Moniak** (57.78), whose massive +14% platoon advantage against Cade Cavalli makes him a safer play for daily efficiency. We are also monitoring the availability of **Josh Naylor**, who is currently staring down an elite arm in Zack Wheeler; while his score of 47.41 is marginal, his established role in the heart of the order keeps him in the lineup despite the -19% SP skill penalty.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for all starters. Specifically, if **Gabriel Moreno** or **Travis Bazzana** are dropped to the bottom third of the batting order, their efficiency scores will crater, necessitating a shift toward bench depth. We are also keeping a close eye on **Zach McKinstry** (40.98), whose value is currently bolstered by favorable winds; should the weather shift at first pitch, he is the most likely candidate to be benched to protect our caps. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Tyler Soderstrom** remain inactive, the rest of our roster, including **James Wood**, **Jose Caballero**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, and **Edwin Arroyo**, will remain on standby as we navigate this high-stakes 5x5 Roto stretch.",
